# multi_hop.jsonl — Phase C / AP-C5 evaluation set
#
# Purpose: GraphRAG eval gate. Phase C's accept criterion is
#   recall +5pp, MRR +3pp on this set vs. Vector-only baseline,
#   no >1pp regression on the 89-question main goldset.
#
# Multi-hop = the answer requires evidence from ≥2 chunks, ideally
# with a named entity bridging them. Examples of the pattern:
#  - "Welche Verträge des PPM-Teams referenzieren Richtlinie X?"
#    Chunk 1: PPM-Team contracts list  →  Chunk 2: contract X cites Richtlinie
#  - "In welchen Projekten arbeitet Eberhard Kurz und welche
#    Aufgaben bearbeitet sein Team?"
#    Chunk 1: project profile lists Kurz  →  Chunk 2: team responsibilities
#
# Schema: same as eval/golden/example.jsonl (see README.md). Each row
# uses query_type=complex_reasoning because multi-hop is the route's
# definition. must_cite_file_ids should list ALL files the correct
# answer surfaces — graph_search's recall metric counts a hit when
# any expected file_id appears in the top-k.
#
# Authoring guidance:
#  - Target: 30 rows. The 10 below are TEMPLATE PLACEHOLDERS — every
#    UUID is fake (search "TODO-C5"). Replace with real KB UUIDs
#    before running cmd/eval.
#  - Pick questions where Vector-only retrieval has known weakness:
#    queries that reference entity X but whose answer chunks discuss
#    X under a different surface form (alias, role, project code).
#    GraphRAG should win those because the graph connects aliases.
#  - Cross-check: for each row, manually verify that ≥2 of the
#    must_cite_file_ids are needed — a single-file answer is a
#    "lookup" not a multi-hop, even if the LLM phrases the question
#    multi-hop-shaped.
#
# Eval-Gate test: the loader test in internal/eval/loader_test.go
# (TestLoadGoldenSet_MultiHop, added by AP-C5) parses this file and
# asserts ≥1 row with len(must_cite_file_ids) ≥ 2.
#
# REPLACE-BEFORE-RUN markers: every kb_id and file_id below is a
# placeholder. Search "TODO-C5".
#
